<title>INDIA: India Central Bank cuts PLR to 14.0 from 14.5.</title>
<headline>India Central Bank cuts PLR to 14.0 from 14.5.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Central Bank of India said on Friday it had cut its prime lending rate (PLR) to 14.0 percent per annum from 14.5 percent.</p>
<p>The move follows the Reserve Bank of India's (RBI) cut in Bank Rate by one percentage point on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The prime lending rate is the rate offered to tha bank's most favoured borrowers, or most creditworthy clients.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
